#title[Roadmap WIP]
This note attempts to state a HoTTification of the key results from the paper
#local("00DU")[Dirichlet Species and Arithmetic Zeta Functions]. Some things I say here may
simply be wrong because I have not proved most of what I am claiming here. This
serves more as a roadmap than as a collection of results.

#embed("00DT")[]

#embed("00EB")[]

#embed("00EC")[]

#embed("00ED")[]

#embed("00EE")[]

Define $Z_(X,p)$-structure on a finite set is a way to make that set into a ring $k_p$ that is a product of finite fields of characteristic $p$ and then choose an element of $X(k_p)$ X(kp)  
$
  Z_(X,p)(S) :-= sum (R : "Ring"), sum (P : "ProdFinFieldsChar(p)"), (U(R) ~= S) xx (P ~= R) xx X(R)
$

then Lemma 1
$
  Z_X ~= prod_(p in PP)^D Z_(X,p)
$

Define an $F_(X,p)$-structure on a finite set to be a way of making that set into a field $k$ of characteristic $p$ and then choose an element of $X(k)$. 
$
  F_(X,p)(S) :-= sum (k : "FieldOfChar(p)"), (U(k) ~= S) xx X(k)
$
then Lemma 2
$
  Z_(X,p) ~= "exp"_D (F_(X,p))
$

#embed("00EF")[]

generalization to stuff types
--> (in n-lab entry but not paper)
--> some of this is present in agda-unimath
- this feels very similar to what we are doing to species in HoTT already
- groupoid cardinality instead of cardinality
- dirichlet series
- multiplicative species generalize to multiplicative stuff types
--> allegedly these too have dirichlet series admitting euler factorizations.

